java.io

IO streams:
========= 
 - In java, io streams represents stream of input and output.

Stream :
=======

- A stream represents a sequence of bytes or characters that can be read from a file/resource or written
 to file/resource . I/O streams are used for input and output files, network connections, and in-memory
 buffers.
 - When an application reads a stream of data from a file or any datasource , it is called input stream.
 - When an application sends/writes stream of data to a file or any other datasource, it is called output stream.
 
 
 There are two different types of streams:
 1. Character Streams :
 ======================
 
 Read or writes the character data, character by character.
 - Character Stream classes are used to read and write character data.
 
 File Class:
 -----------
 - File Class is present in java.io package
 - File class has 2 different constructors:
 
 File(String name):
 ----------------
 - creates a file object with the given name in argument
    
     File file = new File("filename"); // just naming the file
     File file1 = new File("c:\\JFS51\\file1.txt"); // naming and giving the location to the Files.
     
 Construtor:
 -----------
 - File(dir,"filename");
 - This constructor is used to create a file in the specified directory.
 - First argument is the name of the directory,second argument is the name of the file.
 
 Methods:
 ---------
 - exists(): returns true if the file/directory exists.
 
 - createNewFile(): creates a empty file, returns true if created , false if already exsits.
 
 - mkdir(): to create a directory.
 
 - isFile(): to check if it is file or not.
 
 - isDirectory(): returns true if file object points to the directory.
 
 - list(): returns String[] of file/directory names.
 
 - length(): returns the size of a file in bytes.
 
 - delete(): deletes the file or empty directory.
 
 FileWriter:
 -----------
 - FileWriter class allows you to write the data to a file.
 - It internally extends an abstract calss Writer.
 - It has multiple overloaded constructors.
 FileWriter(String filename);
 FileWriter(String filename, boolean append);
 FileWriter(File f);
 FileWriter(File file,boolean append);  
 
